WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.636 --> 00:00:14.297
Life at Patty's Place continued pleasantly enough.

2
00:00:15.217 --> 00:00:20.420
The nights grew cold, but on Friday evenings, the big living room was warm and crowded with guests,

3
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:22.861
laughing and talking until late at night.

4
00:00:23.941 --> 00:00:26.202
Gilbert came occasionally on Friday evenings.

5
00:00:27.162 --> 00:00:31.713
He always seemed to have a good time, but he spoke to Anne politely, the way a new

6
00:00:31.773 --> 00:00:32.393
friend would.

7
00:00:33.194 --> 00:00:35.596
Their old camaraderie was gone entirely.

8
00:00:37.097 --> 00:00:40.740
One rainy winter's day, Anne was leaving Redmond to go home.

9
00:00:41.601 --> 00:00:45.144
The wind suddenly blew strongly, turning her umbrella inside out.

10
00:00:46.205 --> 00:00:51.529
Anne was clutching at it frantically when a voice close to her said, "Pardon me, may I offer

11
00:00:51.569 --> 00:00:53.011
you the shelter of my umbrella?"

12
00:00:53.851 --> 00:00:54.512
Anne looked up.

13
00:00:55.424 --> 00:01:02.247
A tall, handsome man with dark, melancholy eyes— the hero of Anne's dreams—stood before her.

14
00:01:02.267 --> 00:01:05.608
"Thank you," Anne said.

15
00:01:05.628 --> 00:01:09.930
"Let's hurry over to that little building," suggested the stranger.

16
00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:12.931
"We can wait there until this shower is over."

17
00:01:13.792 --> 00:01:17.033
The man's words were very ordinary, but his voice!

18
00:01:17.473 --> 00:01:18.414
And his smile!

19
00:01:19.314 --> 00:01:21.235
Anne felt her heart beating strangely.

20
00:01:22.295 --> 00:01:23.436
They hurried to the building.

21
00:01:24.872 --> 00:01:27.313
The raindrops sparkled on Anne's shining hair.

22
00:01:28.313 --> 00:01:31.214
Her cheeks were flushed, and her eyes big and starry.

23
00:01:33.574 --> 00:01:37.495
The man looked at her admiringly, and Anne blushed under his gaze.

24
00:01:38.556 --> 00:01:43.877
"We are schoolmates, I see," he said, indicating Anne's jacket with the school crest.

25
00:01:44.957 --> 00:01:46.378
"My name is Roy Gardner."

26
00:01:46.398 --> 00:01:50.699
"Sorry, but I don't recognize you," said Anne frankly.

27
00:01:50.719 --> 00:01:56.064
"I studied at Redmond for two years," Roy said, "and then I went to Europe.

28
00:01:57.105 --> 00:01:59.725
I've come back to do the last year of my arts degree."

29
00:02:01.386 --> 00:02:03.466
Roy walked Anne home to Patty's Place.

30
00:02:04.847 --> 00:02:08.308
Before he left, he arranged to visit Anne the following Friday.

31
00:02:09.308 --> 00:02:13.249
Later that evening a box arrived at Patty's Place for "Miss Shirley."

32
00:02:14.189 --> 00:02:17.190
It contained a dozen magnificent red roses.

33
00:02:18.291 --> 00:02:20.111
Phil impertinently read the card.

34
00:02:20.131 --> 00:02:22.072
"Roy Gardner!"

35
00:02:22.552 --> 00:02:23.272
she exclaimed.

36
00:02:24.184 --> 00:02:27.946
"Why, Anne, I didn't know you were acquainted with Roy Gardner!"

37
00:02:27.966 --> 00:02:32.749
"I met him this afternoon in the rain," explained Anne.

38
00:02:32.769 --> 00:02:37.752
"My umbrella turned inside out and he came to my rescue with his."

39
00:02:37.772 --> 00:02:42.254
"Oh." Phil looked suspiciously at Anne.

40
00:02:42.274 --> 00:02:45.976
"And so, naturally, he sent you roses!

41
00:02:47.097 --> 00:02:48.718
I smell romance!"

42
00:02:49.719 --> 00:02:51.880
"Nonsense!" Anne replied stiffly.

43
00:02:52.884 --> 00:02:56.045
But she lay awake a long time that night thinking about Roy.

44
00:02:56.845 --> 00:02:58.926
Perhaps her prince had come at last.

45
00:03:01.006 --> 00:03:04.087
Over the next few months, Anne and Roy became a couple.

46
00:03:05.007 --> 00:03:09.409
Roy came to Patty's Place every Friday night, and Gilbert stopped coming.

47
00:03:10.329 --> 00:03:13.390
Roy and Anne went to all the college events and parties together.

48
00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:19.831
He regularly sent her flowers and was always sure to murmur a poetic compliment whenever he took her

49
00:03:19.872 --> 00:03:21.372
hand or helped her with her coat.

50
00:03:22.916 --> 00:03:27.238
Spring came and the girls at Patty's Place were dressing for the Redmond Spring Dance.

51
00:03:28.218 --> 00:03:30.779
Anne looked at herself in the mirror with satisfaction.

52
00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:33.741
She had a particularly pretty gown on.

53
00:03:34.621 --> 00:03:40.544
Originally it had been only a simple chiffon dress, but Phil had embroidered tiny rosebuds all over the

54
00:03:40.564 --> 00:03:43.125
chiffon and now it was simply stunning.

55
00:03:44.545 --> 00:03:48.687
Anne was trying to fasten a little gold chain around her neck when Phil came in.

56
00:03:48.707 --> 00:03:54.195
"By the way, Anne, Gilbert Blythe has been seen constantly with Christine Stuart.

57
00:03:54.855 --> 00:03:55.436
Did you know?"

58
00:03:56.396 --> 00:03:59.959
Suddenly Anne's fingers didn't work, and she couldn't put the necklace on.

59
00:03:59.979 --> 00:04:03.722
"No, I hadn't heard," she said carelessly.

60
00:04:03.742 --> 00:04:05.984
"Who is Christine Stuart?"

61
00:04:07.685 --> 00:04:10.568
"Christine Stuart transferred to Redmond this semester.

62
00:04:11.428 --> 00:04:14.991
She studied music at a university in Toronto," Phil replied.

63
00:04:15.011 --> 00:04:20.556
"I haven't seen her, but they say she's very pretty and that Gilbert is quite crazy over her.

64
00:04:21.544 --> 00:04:23.765
I was so angry when you refused Gilbert, Anne!

65
00:04:24.485 --> 00:04:26.245
But Roy Gardner was meant for you.

66
00:04:26.325 --> 00:04:27.406
I can see that now.

67
00:04:28.266 --> 00:04:29.326
You were right, after all."

68
00:04:31.247 --> 00:04:34.688
Anne suddenly felt dull, and Phil's chatter seemed trivial.

69
00:04:35.548 --> 00:04:40.469
At the dance Anne danced many times with Roy, but she was acutely conscious of Gilbert.

70
00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:45.391
He stood across the room, talking to a girl who must have been Christine Stuart.

71
00:04:46.251 --> 00:04:51.285
She was lovely, with a pale complexion, long dark hair, and rosy red lips.

72
00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:57.048
Anne was not sorry when the evening ended, and everyone went home.

73
00:04:58.249 --> 00:05:01.671
Phil and Anne made hot chocolate and stayed up late discussing the night.

74
00:05:01.691 --> 00:05:06.113
"All of Redmond knows that Roy is crazy about you, Anne!

75
00:05:06.974 --> 00:05:09.075
And you've been going out for nearly six months now!"

76
00:05:09.535 --> 00:05:10.536
said Phil candidly.

77
00:05:10.556 --> 00:05:13.037
"You're going to marry Roy, aren't you?"

78
00:05:13.057 --> 00:05:16.519
"Phil, he hasn't even asked me!"

79
00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:17.460
Anne said.

80
00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:20.161
"You do love him, don't you, Anne?"

81
00:05:20.561 --> 00:05:21.262
Phil asked.

82
00:05:22.202 --> 00:05:24.243
"I I suppose so."

83
00:05:25.184 --> 00:05:28.606
Anne realized she was confessing her love for Roy for the first time.

84
00:05:29.526 --> 00:05:32.067
But strangely, she felt stiff inside.

85
00:05:32.908 --> 00:05:38.271
Why had her face gone red that evening every time she'd seen Gilbert Blythe and Christine Stuart together?

86
00:05:40.292 --> 00:05:43.074
After Phil went to bed, Anne thought about Roy.

87
00:05:43.094 --> 00:05:45.175
"Of course, I love him.

88
00:05:45.935 --> 00:05:47.216
Roy is my ideal.

89
00:05:48.068 --> 00:05:53.972
Who could resist those glorious dark eyes, his melancholic voice, his handsome looks?"

90
00:05:55.013 --> 00:05:57.715
Anne knew that half the girls at Redmond were envious of her.

91
00:05:58.796 --> 00:06:00.517
And Roy had written poems for her!

92
00:06:01.398 --> 00:06:06.061
Admittedly, he did copy them from magazines, but they were good poems, and very romantic!

93
00:06:07.642 --> 00:06:09.203
Anne began thinking about Gilbert.

94
00:06:09.924 --> 00:06:14.967
Gilbert, she knew, would never write her poems, but on the other hand, Gilbert would always understand a

95
00:06:15.008 --> 00:06:21.459
joke. The day before, Anne had told Roy a very funny story, but he had only smiled politely

96
00:06:21.519 --> 00:06:22.379
and didn't laugh.

97
00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:28.503
Anne recalled telling Gilbert the same story a long time ago and both of them laughing about it

98
00:06:28.543 --> 00:06:29.203
for ages.

99
00:06:32.045 --> 00:06:36.207
Anne wondered uneasily if life with a man who had no sense of humor might be boring.

100
00:06:37.047 --> 00:06:43.091
But who could expect a handsome, melancholy, romantic hero who wrote her poems to see the funny side

101
00:06:43.111 --> 00:06:43.611
of things?

102
00:06:44.451 --> 00:06:45.572
It was too much to ask!

103
00:06:46.437 --> 00:06:51.566
Anne put thoughts of Gilbert out of her head, and went to sleep dreaming of Roy's dark, soulful

104
00:06:51.807 --> 00:06:51.947
eyes.
